  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-ActionKind">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:ActionKind</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-ActionKind"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-023</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: schema.org's subtypes of Action (to verify) have no clone or fast-forward, and Git's commands are the nearest names but no vocabulary. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#ActionKind</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-ExitStatus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:ExitStatus</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-ExitStatus"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0025-ifws FR-010</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: POSIX gives 0 for success and non-zero for failure, and the BSD header sysexits.h gives named codes (EX_OK 0, EX_USAGE 64, EX_UNAVAILABLE 69, EX_SOFTWARE 70, EX_CONFIG 78 and others); none gives ok, findings, usage and environment as 0 to 3. IFWS's 0, 1, 2 and 3 follow the shell convention (1 is a general failure, here findings; 2 is a misuse of the command, as in the Bash builtins and GNU tools), not sysexits.h, whose usage code is 64; the four values are few, kept apart on purpose, and a caller reads them without a table. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#ExitStatus</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-Finding">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:Finding</rdfs:label>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Maps"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-035</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>SARIF 2.1.0 defines a result (ruleId, level, message, locations) and has no RDF vocabulary, so the mapping is a JSON Schema pointer; the finding adds the day it was first seen</mz:justification>
    <mz:mappingRelation>closeMatch</mz:mappingRelation>
    <mz:standardTerm>https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json#/definitions/result</mz:standardTerm>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#Finding</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-GeneratedFile">
