  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-GitCapability">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:GitCapability</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-GitCapability"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-016</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: None found: OpenAPI describes the operations of one API, not a list of capabilities that hosts support or lack. ForgeFed (to verify) models forge objects, not what a client may ask. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#GitCapability</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-GitManager">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:GitManager</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-GitManager"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-015</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: ForgeFed (a federation vocabulary of forges, repositories and tickets; to verify) and schema:WebAPI (to verify): neither names a client-side interface to GitHub, GitLab and plain Git with a set of capabilities, one of which may be unsupported. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#GitManager</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-GitManagerKind">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:GitManagerKind</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-GitManagerKind"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-016</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: GitHub, GitLab and Git are products and projects: no standard vocabulary lists them as a code list. SPDX 3 and DOAP name a repository's kind of version control, not the host (to verify). Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#GitManagerKind</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-Module">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:Module</rdfs:label>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Specializes"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0025-ifws FR-003</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>The convention of the executable `ifws-&lt;name&gt;` on the path is Git's `git-foo`</mz:justification>
    <mz:mappingRelation>subClassOf</mz:mappingRelation>
    <mz:standardTerm>https://schema.org/SoftwareApplication</mz:standardTerm>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#Module</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-ModuleSource">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:ModuleSource</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-ModuleSource"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0025-ifws FR-004</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: Git's external-command convention (`git-foo` on the PATH) names the third source and no standard lists the other two or their order. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#ModuleSource</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
