  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-RepoState">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:RepoState</rdfs:label>
    <mz:addedOn>2026-11-17</mz:addedOn>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Unaligned"/>
    <mz:decision rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/decision-ifws-RepoState"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-022</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>No standard adopted yet. Examined: Git's `git status --porcelain=v2 --branch` reports the branch head, its upstream and the ahead and behind counts, and Git documents locks and a detached HEAD, but Git publishes no vocabulary of states; missing, wrong remote and not a repository are the workspace's. Kept unaligned by the owner's decision of 2026-11-17 (issue #10); reviewed again by 2027-02-15.</mz:justification>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#RepoState</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/id/mizan/term-ifws-Repository">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#OntologyTerm"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ifws:Repository</rdfs:label>
    <mz:basis rdf:resource="https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/mizan#Maps"/>
    <mz:definedBy>0023-if-workspaces FR-006</mz:definedBy>
    <mz:justification>DOAP's GitRepository is a published repository with a location; the workspace's Repository is its clone at a path that mirrors that location, so the match is close and not exact. schema:SoftwareSourceCode and dcat:Dataset were examined and describe the content, not the clone</mz:justification>
    <mz:mappingRelation>closeMatch</mz:mappingRelation>
    <mz:standardTerm>http://usefulinc.com/ns/doap#GitRepository</mz:standardTerm>
    <mz:termIri>https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifws#Repository</mz:termIri>
  </rdf:Description>
